course: dictionary
lesson: 7735
title: Pullover: a jumper for cold days
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A pullover is a knitted top with sleeves that you pull on over your head. Most people call it a jumper or a sweater. Context helps you spot it: «Granny knits a woolly pullover» tells you it is warm and made of wool, and the words woolly and knits are clues.
explain: Pullovers come in different styles. «A V-neck pullover» has a neck shaped like the letter V, and «a school pullover» is part of a school uniform. When you see a word like pullover in a maths problem, such as «A pullover costs $15 in a 20% off sale», the numbers tell you it is an item you can buy.
explain: Pullover has a second, rare meaning: anything that is pulled over something else. This is much less common, so when you read the word in clothes stories, it almost always means the jumper. If the sentence is about cold weather or school, check the context before deciding.
fact: A pullover is a knitted top that you pull on over your head.
fact: A pullover is also called a jumper or a sweater.
fact: «A woolly pullover» means a pullover made of wool, which is warm.
fact: «A V-neck pullover» has a neck shaped like the letter V.
fact: Pullover has a rare second meaning: anything pulled over something else.
fact: The French word «un pull» means a jumper. It was borrowed from the English word pullover and made shorter.
exercise: Granny knits «a woolly pullover» for the cold winter. What is a pullover? | A bag for school books | *A knitted top you pull on over your head | A pair of trousers with a belt | A hat with a bobble on top
exercise: «She wore her school pullover to the maths lesson.» What does school pullover tell you? | *It is a jumper that is part of the school uniform | It is a coat for the summer | It is a sports bag for swimming | It is a book about school
exercise: The French word «un pull» means a jumper. Which English word was it borrowed from? | pull-up | *pullover | pillow | pudding
test: «A pullover costs $15 in a 20% off sale.» In this sentence, what does the 20% off tell you? | The colour of the pullover | The size of the pullover | The number of pullovers in the shop | *The discount, so the price goes down
test: Which is the rare meaning of pullover? | A jumper with long sleeves | A pair of shoes | A school bag | *Anything pulled over something else
exam: Which sentence uses pullover correctly? | I pullover my bike to school every day | *On cold mornings I put on my woolly pullover before I go out | We pullover the big dog in the park | The pullover was sunny and warm at the beach
